{
  "trial": "A2 Il1r1 dosage against the Wnt programme",
  "rules_frozen_at": "2026-09-20T08:13:48+00:00",
  "rules": {
    "question": "does deleting Il1r1 move the Wnt programme in Kras-mutant AT2-derived clones",
    "why_route_A_was_impossible": "England 2025's Figure S2L-N, the only direct measurement of Axin2 and Il1r1 overlap in the literature, was never deposited: the superseries and both subseries contain zero mentions of ZsGreen and the NCBI link service returns three series for that paper, none holding the sorted libraries",
    "what_is_asked_instead": "the untested half of the crosstalk Choi 2020 hypothesised. IL-1 to Wnt in AT2 is not established anywhere; the reverse, Wnt inducing IL-1beta, is established by Aumiller 2013 and almost never cited",
    "the_ceiling": "two libraries per group; under a permutation of four labels into two groups of two there are six orderings, so the smallest attainable p is 1/6 and nothing here can be significant. The trial computes no p value and reports complete separation or its absence",
    "R1_unit": "the library; mice per library are not reported in GEO so the mouse-level n is unknown and not assumed",
    "R2_label_corroboration": "Il1r1 must be lower in both homozygous libraries than in both heterozygous ones, checked before any Wnt quantity",
    "R3_readout": "pseudobulk Wnt target module (Axin2, Nkd1, Tcf7l2, Lef1, Notum, Wif1) as summed counts over summed totals per 10,000",
    "R4_null": "300 random six-gene modules matched on total expression within a factor of two",
    "R5_reading": "complete separation and clearing the null; complete separation only; neither; or R2 failing",
    "register_status": "Descriptive only whatever it finds"
  },
